SIMPLE  =                    T / conforms to FITS standard                      BITPIX  =                  -64 / array data type                                NAXIS   =                    2 / number of array dimensions                     NAXIS1  =                 1024                                                  NAXIS2  =                 1024                                                  COMMENT FITS (Flexible Image Transport System) format is defined in 'Astronomy  COMMENT and Astrophysics', volume 376, page 359; bibcode 2001A&A...376..359H    COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT DESCRIPTION:                                                            COMMENT  This file contains a measured, on-orbit WFE from 2022 July 30          COMMENT  selected to be a representative but slightly conservative OPD          COMMENT  for in-flight performance.                                             COMMENT  In particular it is the WFE after a couple weeks of relative stability COMMENT  and just before a mirror correction.                                   COMMENT  This is about a 75th percentile wavefront, as measured during the firstCOMMENT  few months of cycle 1.                                                 COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT  This is the same OPD that will be used in the JWST ETC for Cycle 2     COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT IMPORTANT NOTE ABOUT INTERPRETING WAVEFRONT ERROR VALUES:               COMMENT  One must be careful to specify exactly what a given WFE                COMMENT  measurement refers to, and to distinguish contributing terms.          COMMENT  In particular, this file, from O2022073001-NRCA3_FP1-1.fits,           COMMENT  was measured at NIRCam NRCA3 field point 1 ('FP1').                    COMMENT  At that field point the combined OTE+NRC WFE had:                      COMMENT      WFE_(OTE+NRC) = 76.2 nm rms                                        COMMENT  If the NIRCam SI WFE at that field point, known from ground tests,     COMMENT  is subtracted off, the resulting WFE has:                              COMMENT      WFE_(OTE, at FP1) = 67.2 nm rms                                    COMMENT  That is the WFE which the WF control system maintains.                 COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT  Because of how WebbPSF handles WFE terms, this file also subtracts off COMMENT  the OTE field dependence, to yield the WFE at a central field point    COMMENT  in between the two NIRCam modules. This has                            COMMENT     WFE_(OTE, center FP) = 71.2 nm rms                                  COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT  These all refer to the same overall state of the observatory.          FILECONT= 'Analysis output products' /                                          TSTAMP  = '2022-07-30T23:01:31' /                                               DATE-OBS= '2022-07-30'         /                                                TIME-OBS= '14:16:12.830'       /                                                OBS_ID  = 'V02586024001P0000000003104' /                                        OP_TYPE = 'FINE_PHASING'       /                                                MODE    = 'MANUAL  '           /                                                OPER    = 'TRUE    '           /                                                CORR_ID = 'O2022073001'        /                                                GROUP_ID=                    1 /                                                GRP_CNT =                    2 /                                                INSTRUME= 'Any     '           / OPD for OTE exit pupil; can be used with any SIDETECTOR= 'NRCA3   '           /                                                APERNAME= 'NRCA3_FP1'          /                                                FPX     =             -1.16891 /                                                FPY     =            -0.767005 /                                                BUNIT   = 'micron  '           / OPD given in microns of path delay             PUPLDIAM=             6.603464 / Pupil *file* size in meters per side [m]       PUPLSCAL=      0.0064486953125 / Pupil pixel scale  [meter/pixel]               CONTENTS= 'Estimated OTE WFE from Wavefront Sensing Measurements'               SOFTWARE= '"Prepare Example Cycle 1 OPD file.ipynb" by Perrin'                  DATE    = '2022-09-21T15:28:11.769' / Time file was written                     ORIENT  = '+Y axis is +V3, +X axis is +V2' / Looking into OTE entrance pupil    DIAM_CRC=             6.603464 / OTE circumscribing circle diameter [m]         DIAM_FLT=             6.559348 / Flat-to-flat distance across pupil in V3 axis  WFE_RMS =                71.48 /  [nm] RMS wavefront error, but see COMMENTS    WFELEVEL= 'Measured'           / Measured WFE, from Cycle 1 wavefront sensing   AUTHOR  = 'Marshall Perrin'                                                     HISTORY OPD file retrieved from MAST for use by WebbPSF.                        HISTORY Converting input for use with WebbPSF:                                  HISTORY Input file is: O2022073001-NRCA3_FP1-1.fits                             HISTORY   Retrieved from MAST JWST_WSS data repository.                         HISTORY   Need to rescale from 256x256 to 1024x1024 pixels.                     HISTORY   Dilated OPD values to fill adjacent invalid pixels (i.e. fill in gaps)HISTORY   Interpolated array to 1024x1024 pixels across                         HISTORY   Converted units from microns to meters                                HISTORY Estimating SI WFE at sensing field point NRCA3_FP1.                     HISTORY   See FITS extension SENSING_SI_WFE for the SI WFE model used.          